            "Most real projects mix both columns. Building a new office is predictive at its core, but the workplace design, move communications and IT set-up can be run iteratively. Launching a regulated product has fixed submission steps, but marketing content and training can be built in sprints. A hybrid plan, with a predictive backbone and Agile delivery inside it, is often the right answer. Our [Agile vs Waterfall guide](/project-management/agile/agile-vs-waterfall/) compares the two approaches in detail.",
