            H3("Step 2: Limit work in progress"),
            "With WIP limits in place, the team stops starting new vacancies when a column is full and helps move existing ones forward instead, for example by chasing interview feedback. Lower-priority vacancies wait in Approved, visibly, so hiring managers can see the queue and the team can agree priorities with them. Our guide to [WIP limits](/project-management/kanban/wip-limits/) explains how to set them.",
